  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Tool You Already Know",
    "overview": "QR & Barcode Studio looks like the category leaders on purpose. Cool grey ground, white panels drawn with 1px hairlines, slate ink and one blue: a visitor who has used QRCode Monkey or QR Code Generator recognises every control before reading a label. Familiarity is the design decision, not a fallback; the craft goes into finish (exact alignment, honest states, AA contrast, 44px targets) rather than into novelty.\n\nThe density is operational. One short task per visit, so the code is the hero and the chrome stays quiet: the live preview sits on a neutral grey stage beside the settings and stays in view while they change, and one blue button downloads it. Controls feel native because they are: segmented choices are real radio buttons, long lists are native selects, the colour field opens a real picker, sliders and checkboxes are platform inputs tinted blue. The dark theme mirrors the same structure on slate, keeping the action blue unchanged.\n\nThis world replaced the previous look and rejects it explicitly: no indigo-to-violet gradients, no emoji headings, no cards nested in cards, no bouncy motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One accent: Action Blue for the primary action, selection and focus; everything else is grey and slate.",
      "Flat white panels on a cool grey ground, separated by 1px hairlines with a barely-there shadow.",
      "Inter at a fixed rem ramp (0.75rem to 2rem); weight carries most of the hierarchy.",
      "Monospace with tabular numerals only for data: hex values, access keys, CNPJ, scanned text.",
      "Native-feeling controls at 44px minimum; the primary action and mode switch at 48px.",
      "Quiet functional motion: 150ms ease-out state changes, short entries for floating layers, nothing loops or overshoots."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Action Blue fills exactly one button per view, the primary action. Selection and focus may use blue; secondary actions (Copiar, Copiar texto, WhatsApp, Facebook, Enviar imagem) stay neutral grey.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Code Is Content Rule",
        "body": "The colours a person picks for their QR Code or barcode, and the template presets that set them, belong to the code, not to the palette. The stage around the code stays neutral grey so any user colour reads true, and the system never tints, overlays or decorates the code itself.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Ramp Rule",
        "body": "Sizes are fixed rem steps between 0.75rem and 2rem, never fluid clamps; hierarchy comes from weight (400 / 500 / 600 / 700) and ink (Slate, Muted, Faint) before size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Means Data Rule",
        "body": "The monospace stack with tabular numerals is reserved for values a person reads character by character: hex colours, NF-e access keys, CNPJ, series and numbers, scanned text. Counts and percentages in proportional text use tabular numerals without switching face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Preview Stays in View Rule",
        "body": "In the generator modes the code is always visible while settings change: sticky beside the settings from 960px, and placed directly after Conteúdo on phones with its download button under it.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline First Rule",
        "body": "A surface earns a border before it earns a shadow; only the rendered code and floating layers get more than the hairline lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Nesting Radius Rule",
        "body": "An element's radius is never larger than its container's: 12 outside, 8 inside, 6 inside that.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reserve Action Blue (#2563eb) for one filled primary button per view, selected states and focus.",
      "Do keep secondary actions neutral: the Panel White secondary button with a Field Stroke border, or the Muted Slate ghost and link buttons with a Sunken Stage hover.",
      "Do divide a panel into sections with a 1px Hairline rule and 1.25rem 1.5rem padding instead of adding an inner card.",
      "Do build choices on the Segmented control over native radios, use native selects for long lists and native checkbox and range inputs tinted with accent-color.",
      "Do keep every interactive target at least 44px tall, and the main action of a view at 48px.",
      "Do set hex values, access keys, CNPJ and scanned text in the mono stack with tabular numerals.",
      "Do keep the rendered code on the neutral Sunken Stage with the Label lift, at its own colours.",
      "Do define every new colour token in both the light `:root` block and the `.dark` block of App.css.",
      "Do animate only colour, border and shadow on state changes (150ms, cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)), and short fades or slides for floating layers, all collapsed under prefers-reduced-motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use gradients on any surface, button, text or icon.",
      "Don't use emoji in headings, labels or buttons; icons are the Ant Design outline set or SVGs drawn to match it.",
      "Don't nest a bordered, shadowed card inside a panel; bordered tiles inside a panel are only for selectable controls like the template tiles.",
      "Don't use bouncy or overshooting easing, or any looping or decorative animation.",
      "Don't colour secondary or text actions blue; blue belongs to the one primary action.",
      "Don't tint, overlay or decorate the code inside the preview stage; scan reliability comes before decoration.",
      "Don't use the legacy alias variables (--text-primary, --text-secondary, --bg-primary, --bg-secondary, --secondary, --border-color) in new CSS; use the base names (--text-main, --text-muted, --bg-panel, --bg-sunken, --border)."
    ]
  }
}